fltime -- automatic time and the time zone helper
================================================

Two small programs for Settings > Date & time. C17, MIT.

fl-sntp (/usr/sbin) is a minimal SNTP client (RFC 4330). The init script
/etc/rc.d/init.d/ntp (initscripts; `ntp` is in SERVICES in /etc/rc.conf) runs it as a
daemon: it asks the servers in /etc/fltime.conf (SERVERS="a b", default pool.ntp.org;
HOST or HOST:PORT), steps the clock when it is 0.2 s or more off, slews it with
adjtime(3) when it is closer, then asks again after an hour. Until the network
answers it retries after 10, 20, 40 ... 300 s. State: /run/fltime.status
(state=synced|waiting, last=, offset_ms=, server=), removed when it stops. The
hardware clock is saved by rc.shutdown. `fl-sntp -q HOST[:PORT]` only asks and prints the
offset (no privileges needed), `-1` asks once and sets the clock.
It answers only to its own question: the reply must echo our transmit time, mode 4,
stratum 1-15, not "alarm"; of three tries the quickest is used.

fltime-set (/usr/bin) is the one privileged part. It is installed setuid root for the
group seat (recipe owner= "/usr/bin/fltime-set 0 98 4750", the same pattern as flpower
and flpkg-seat) and does exactly four things, nothing else:

	fltime-set zone NAME     /etc/localtime -> /usr/share/zoneinfo/NAME, /etc/timezone
	fltime-set ntp on|off    NTP= in /etc/fltime.conf, then restart/stop the ntp service
	fltime-set sync          restart the ntp service now (only while ntp is on)
	fltime-set time EPOCH    set the clock (only while ntp is off), then hwclock --systohc

Checks: NAME has only letters, digits, _ + - . and / with no empty part and no part
that starts with a dot, at most 48 characters, is not under posix/ or right/, and after
realpath(3) is a regular file inside the zoneinfo directory that starts with "TZif";
the links are made with symlink + rename, so /etc/localtime is never missing. EPOCH is
digits only, between 2023 and 2100, and refused while automatic time is on. The
environment is discarded, the paths are compiled in (the tests build a copy with
other paths), the service script runs with a clean environment and no terminal.
Exit status: 0 done, 2 usage, 3 argument refused, 4 refused (ntp state), 1 failed.

Tests: tests/test.sh builds the helper against a scratch directory and fl-sntp against
tests/fakentp.py (a stand-in NTP server) and needs no privileges:
	CC=cc tests/test.sh /usr/share/zoneinfo
Settings' own end-to-end test is src/flsettings/tests/datetime.py.
